Third-party code
================

Parts of the C++ core (cpp/src) are translations of code from the following projects. Their copyright notices and
licenses apply to the corresponding parts.

R package "forecast" (GPL-3)
  Copyright (C) Rob J Hyndman and contributors. https://github.com/robjhyndman/forecast
  Translated: ets() and its likelihood / initialisation (cpp/src/ets.cpp), auto.arima(), ndiffs(), nsdiffs(),
  seas.heuristic(), myarima() and the forecasting chain (cpp/src/autoarima.cpp), tbats() / bats() and their Rcpp
  helpers (cpp/src/tbats.cpp), stlf() / mstl() / forecast.stl() (cpp/src/stlf.cpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/py_sf.py),
  baggedETS() / bld.mbb.bootstrap() / MBB() / BoxCox.lambda() (cpp/src/bagged.cpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/r_boot.py),
  HoltWintersZZ() / zzhw(), forecast.ets()'s class3() and src/etspolyroot.c (R_cpolyroot) (cpp/src/ets.cpp,
  cpp/src/cpoly.cpp).

R package "thief" (GPL-3)
  Copyright (C) Rob J Hyndman and Nikolaos Kourentzes. Translated: thief(), tsaggregates(), th.forecast(),
  reconcilethief() with comb = "struc" (cpp/src/temporal.cpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/py_sf.py).

R package "MAPA" (GPL-2 or later)
  Copyright (C) Nikolaos Kourentzes and Fotios Petropoulos. Translated: mapaest(), mapacalc(), statetranslate(),
  mapacomb() with type = "ets" (cpp/src/temporal.cpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/py_sf.py).

catch22 / R package "Rcatch22" v0.1.13 (GPL-3)
  Copyright (C) Carl H. Lubba, Ben D. Fulcher, Trent Henderson and contributors.
  https://github.com/chlubba/catch22, https://github.com/hendersontrent/Rcatch22
  Included: the C feature code and its helpers, comments removed (cpp/src/catch22/), with a switch reproducing the
  ranking study's Rcatch22 build (unit FFT twiddle factors).

R "stats" package, part of R (GPL-2 or later)
  Copyright (C) The R Core Team. https://www.r-project.org
  Translated: arima() with ARIMA_Like / ARIMA_CSS / getQ0, optim()'s vmmin (BFGS) and nmmin (Nelder-Mead) and
  optimhess (cpp/src/arima.cpp, cpp/src/ets.cpp), stl() / stl.c (cpp/src/autoarima.cpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/r_stl.py),
  optimize() (Brent_fmin), loess() for one predictor (loessc.c / loessf.f by W. S. Cleveland, E. Grosse and
  M. J. Shyu, in cpp/src/loess.cpp and src/tsfstudio/engines/r_loess.py); LINPACK dqrdc / dqrsl / dsvdc (R's src/appl)
  and the reference BLAS of R's src/extra/blas (ddot, daxpy, dscal, drot, dnrm2, drotg) in the same files;
  L-BFGS-B (src/appl/lbfgsb.c, after Zhu, Byrd, Lu & Nocedal), optim()'s lbfgsb driver and finite-difference
  gradient, LINPACK dpofa / dtrsl / dqrdc2 (cpp/src/lbfgsb.cpp, cpp/src/rlinpack.hpp);
  and from R's base sources the Mersenne-Twister seeding, unif_rand() and R_unif_index()
  of src/main/RNG.c, mean() / colMeans() / var() summation (cpp/src/rstats.hpp, src/tsfstudio/engines/r_boot.py).

